Z||000000||fldevel||11-06-2000||01:07 PM||||im getting really low ..sometime erratic idle and engine light come on when it starts idling low or when im downshifting .. im not gettin any errors on the ECM i just get a code 12 ..ive tried everything from replacing vaccume lines to changing the IAC to the MAP senser and nothing .. the car runs excelent untill it starts to warm up ..any ideas ?? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||11-06-2000||01:20 PM||||Sounds like you're getting an intermittent code 35 (IAC)...usually not because of IAC defect, but because idle speed is fluctuating plus or minus 50 rpm.<P>Most common cause is a vacuum leak, but dirty throttle body/intake can cause this. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||william_thorniii||11-06-2000||01:28 PM||||Friends,<P>I have been having a similar problem in my (soon to be sold) 85 GT.  There are neither any trouble codes stored nor do any of the sensors monitored by the ECM see strange signals (according to my OTC).<P>The symptoms are that the check engine light appears when cranking as normal.  Once the engine fires it turns off as normal.  After idling for a few seconds (as normal), the check engine light comes on the first time the engine rev's increase to disengage the clutch.  The car runs excellently, there are no abnormalities that can be detected by ECM, OTC Monitor and/or seat-o-the-pants-o-meter.  <P>Any suggestions?<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
